    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d373">

                <pb facs="0435" n="1169" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1169"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dupuy de Lôme to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Spain</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Boston</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-07-13"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 13,
                    1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have received here the
                    note of Mr. Adee in regard to the Mora claim.</p>
                <p>Before leaving Washington I told Mr. Adee that I had been advised that in a very
                    few days that long-pending question would be settled.</p>
                <p>The Duke of Tetuan has kept me informed by cable of every step of the action
                    taken in regard to that matter. I am sure that a very few days, no more than are
                    necessary to comply with our internal procedure, will bring the final solution
                    of the question.</p>
                <p>So soon as I shall be informed of the proceedings of the cabinet meetings, I
                    shall have the honor to communicate them to you.</p>
                <p>Believe me, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Dupuy de Lôme</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
